**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**2 [[Mr. Angel]]s (200%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since you will have to deal with another level afterwards to actually get the Elder Fruit or Seed, you can use one of these 2 methods to beat this:
# '''Use a centralized lineup for a few specific stages and hope they appear (Very luck-based and inefficient, but MUCH easier.)'''
#*For example, if preparing for [[Galactic Threat (Merciless)|Galactic Threat]] or [[Seas of Death (Merciless)|Seas of Death]], units that can counter Aliens and Zombies comfortably should be used. They'll clear the stages without issue if the time is right, but otherwise they won't hold up at all, cutting consistency to a meager 2/7. The chances can be improved with formation diversity, but in general it's recommended to not factor in [[Clash of Steel (Merciless)|Clash of Steel]], as Metal stages are difficult to clear in general without a fully dedicated strategy.
# '''Go with a more universal lineup that can comfortably take on many stages. (Difficult without good Ubers or high levels, but gets the most out of the stage.)'''
#*Some units, if owned, prove to be spectacular generalists that can work in most of the stages with the proper support, which can save slots for specialists. Again, it's not recommended to build around Clash of Steel unless the units could comfortably handle it.

Here are some units that can help greatly on this stage:
#[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], and/or [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] – good choices for meatshields, with Ramen having extra use against [[Holy Wrath (Merciless)|Holy Wrath]] and Shigong greatly easing [[Seas of Death (Merciless)|Seas of Death]]. These four meatshields are enough to get you through all of the other stages.
#[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], and/or [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Gao]] – powerful spammable attackers, although if using the latter 2, a good [[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|backliner]] for the Angel stage is needed as Ramen cannot solo it without support. In the case of using Cyborg, if you are redoing this stage after obtaining Slapstick Cats, it is most certainly a better option over Cyborg for their better cost efficiency.
#[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] – Required for [[Hearts of Darkness (Merciless)|Hearts of Darkness]], unless you can somehow beat the Razorback with brute force using Ubers.
#[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]], [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]], or [[The 9th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|The 9th Angel]] – using any of these will guarantee a win on the Alien stage, although Cyberpunk must be stacked for best effect.
#[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]], or [[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Tokyo Miku]] – for stalling the Berserkory in the first stage, and to trivialize [[Color of Blood (Merciless)|Color of Blood]]
#Generalist ubers with excellent damage and/or a good crowd-control effect ([[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao]], [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Amaterasu]], [[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Rekon Korps]], [[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Scourge]], [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]], [[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]], [[Wonder MOMOCO (Legend Rare Cat)|Wonder MOMOCO]],[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)| King of Destiny Phonoa]], [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] and/or [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Chronos the Infinite]] to name a few) can help on more than one stage and are a great use of your precious 10 slots.
#[[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]], [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]] or [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]] – critters for the Metal One Horn in the first stage as well as the entirety of the Metal stage. Note that Soba is more consistent for the former with her 100% crit, but the Ubers are more preferred as they have fast Area Attacks.
#[[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]] - A very special Legend Rare with many great abilities, with Critical Hits and Zombie Killer in particular being great for Clash of Steel and Seas of Death respectively.

You must also remember that most [[Battle Items|items]] do not carry over, meaning that Treasure Radars will be useless and you can't get any extra help in the second stage. However, this does open new possibilities, as battle items can be used to compensate deficiencies on An Elder Secret so any remaining units can be dedicated to all continuation stages.

